G0575.def:
**ἀπό** (on the frequently neglect of elision bef. vowels, see Tdf., _Pr._, 94, WH, _App._, 146),
_prep._ with genitive (WM, 462ff.; on its relation to ἐκ, παρά, ὑπό, ib. 456f.), [in LXX for לְ ,בְּ ,מִן ;]
**from** (i.e. from the exterior).
1. **Of separation and cessation**;
(1) **of motion from a place**: [[Mat.5.29, 30; 7.23|Mat.5:29, 30 7:23]], [[Luk.5.2; 22.41|Luk.5:2 22:41]], al.;
(2) in partitive sense (M, _Pr._, 72, 102, 245; MM, see word; Bl., §40, 2), [[Mat.9.16; 27.21|Mat.9:16 27:21]], [[Jhn.21.10|Jhn.21:10]], [[Act.5.2|Act.5:2]], al.; also after verbs of eating, etc.;
(3) of alienation (cl. genitive of separation), after such verbs as λούω (Deiss., _BS_, 227), λύω, σώζω, παύω, etc.; ἀνάθεμα ἀ., [[Rom.9.3|Rom.9:3]] ἀποθνήσκειν ἀ., [[Col.2.20|Col.2:20]] σαλευθῆναι, [[2Th.2.2|2Th.2:2]], καθαρός, -ίζειν, ἀ. (Deiss., _BS_, 196, 216), [[Act.20.26|Act.20:26]], [[2Co.7.1|2Co.7:1]], [[Heb.9.14|Heb.9:14]];
(4) of position, [[Mat.23.34; 24.31|Mat.23:34 24:31]], al.; after μακράν, [[Mat.8.30|Mat.8:30]] transposed before measures of distance, [[Jhn.10.18; 21.8|Jhn.10:18 21:8]], [[Rev.14.20|Rev.14:20]] (Abbott, _JG_, 227);
(5) of time, ἀπὸ τ. ὥρας, ἡμέρας, etc., [[Mat.9.22|Mat.9:22]], [[Jhn.19.27|Jhn.19:27]], [[Act.20.18|Act.20:18]], [[Php.1.5|Php.1:5]], al.; ἀπ᾽ αἰῶνος, [[Luk.1.70|Luk.1:70]], al.; ἀπ᾽ ἀρχῆς, etc., [[Mat.19.4|Mat.19:4]], [[Rom.1.20|Rom.1:20]]; ἀπὸ βρέφους, [[2Ti.3.15|2Ti.3:15]] ἀφ᾽ ἧς, **since**, [[Luk.7.45|Luk.7:45]], al.; ἀπὸ τ. νῦν, [[Luk.1.48|Luk.1:48]], al.; ἀπὸ τότε, [[Mat.4.17|Mat.4:17]], al.; ἀπὸ πέρυσι, **a year ago**, [[2Co.8.10; 9.2|2Co.8:10 9:2]]; ἀπὸ πρωΐ, [[Act.28.23|Act.28:23]]
(6) of order or rank, ἀπὸ διετοῦς, [[Mat.2.16|Mat.2:16]] ἀπὸ Ἀβραάμ, [[Mat.1.17|Mat.1:17]] ἐβδομος ἀπὸ Ἀδάμ, [[Jude.14|Ju 14]]; ἀπὸ μικροῦ ἕως μεγάλου, [[Act.8.10|Act.8:10]], [[Heb.8.11|Heb.8:11]]; ἄρχεσθαι ἀπό, [[Mat.20.8|Mat.20:8]], [[Jhn.8.9|Jhn.8:9]], [[Act.8.35|Act.8:35]], al.
2. **Of origin**;
(1) of birth, extraction, and hence, in late writers,
(a) of local extraction (cl. ἐξ; Abbott, _JG_, 227ff.), [[Mat.21.11|Mat.21:11]], [[Mrk.15.43|Mrk.15:43]], [[Jhn.1.45|Jhn.1:45]], [[Act.10.38|Act.10:38]], al.; οἱ ἀπὸ Ἰταλίας (WM, §66, 6; M, _Pr._, 237; Westc, Rendall, in l.), [[Heb.13.24|Heb.13:24]]
(b) of membership in a community or society (BL, §40, 2), [[Act.12.1|Act.12:1]], al.;
(with) of material (= cl. genitive; Bl. l.with; M, _Pr._, 102), [[Mat.3.4; 27.21|Mat.3:4 27:21]];
(d) after verbs of asking, seeking, etc., [[Luk.11.50, 51|Luk.11:50, 51]] [[1Th.2.6|1Th.2:6]] (Milligan, in l.);
(2) of the cause, instrument, means or occasion (frequently = ὑπό, παρά, and after verbs of learning, hearing, knowing, etc.; Bl., §40, 3), [[Mat.7.16; 11.29|Mat.7:16 11:29]], [[Luk.22.45|Luk.22:45]], [[Act.2.22; 4.36; 9.13; 12.14|Act.2:22 4:36 9:13 12:14]], [[1Co.11.23|1Co.11:23]], [[Gal.3.2|Gal.3:2]], al.; ἀπὸ τ. ὄχλου, [[Luk.19.3|Luk.19:3]] (cf. [[Jhn.21.6|Jhn.21:6]], [[Act.22.11|Act.22:11]]); ἀπὸ τ. φόβου, [[Mat.14.26|Mat.14:26]], al. (cf. [[Mat.10.26; 13.44|Mat.10:26 13:44]]).
3. **Noteworthy Hellenistic phrases**: φοβεῖσθαι ἀπό (M, _Pr._, 102, 107); προσέχειν ἀπό (M, _Pr._, 11. with; Milligan, _NTD_, 50); ἀπὸ νότου (Heb. מִגֶּנֶב), [[Rev.21.13|Rev.21:13]] ἀπὸ προσώπου (מִפְּנֵי), [[2Th.1.9|2Th.1:9]] (Bl., §40, 9); ἀπὸ τ. καρδιῶν (בְּלֵב), [[Mat.18.35|Mat.18:35]] ἀπὸ ὁ ὤν (WM, §10, 2; M, _Pr._, 9), [[Rev.1.4|Rev.1:4]]
4. In composition, ἀπό denotes separation, departure, origin, etc. (ἀπολύω, ἀπέρχομαι, ἀπογράφω); it also has a perfective force (M, _Pr._, 112, 247), as in ἀφικνεῖσθαι, which see
(AS)

G0514.def:
**ἄξιος**, -α, -ον
(ἄγω, in sense, to weigh), [in LXX for בֵּן ([[Deu.25.2|Deu.25:2]]), מָלֵא, שָׁוָה; frequently in Wis, 2Mac ;]
1. **Part One **
(a) of weight, worth (often with genitive, cf. Pr 315, 811), before πρός: [[Rom.8.18|Rom.8:18]] (see Field, _Notes_, 157);
(b) **befitting, meet**: with genitive, [[Mat.3.8|Mat.3:8]], [[Luk.3.8; 23.41|Luk.3:8 23:41]], [[Act.26.20|Act.26:20]], [[1Co.16.4|1Co.16:4]] (see M, _Pr._, 216); absol., [[2Th.1.3|2Th.1:3]]
(with) of persons, **worthy**;
2. **Part Two**
α **in good sense**: with genitive of thing(s), [[Mat.10.10|Mat.10:10]], [[Luk.7.4; 10.7|Luk.7:4 10:7]], [[Act.13.46|Act.13:46]], [[1Ti.1.15; 4.9; 5.18; 6.1|1Ti.1:15 4:9 5:18 6:1]]; with aor. inf. (see M, _Pr._, 203): [[Luk.15.19, 21|Luk.15:19, 21]], Act_13:25, [[Rev.4.11; 5.2, 4; 5.9, 12|Rev.4:11 5:2, 4 5:9, 12]]; before ἵνα: [[Jhn.1.27|Jhn.1:27]] ἅς, [[Luk.7.4|Luk.7:4]] absol., but of what understood: [[Mat.10.11, 13; 22.8|Mat.10:11, 13 22:8]], [[Rev.3.4|Rev.3:4]]; with genitive of person(s), [[Mat.10.37-38|Mat.10:37-38]], [[Heb.11.38|Heb.11:38]];
β **in bad sense**; with genitive of thing(s), [[Luk.12.48; 23.15|Luk.12:48 23:15]], [[Act.23.29; 25.11, 25; 26.31|Act.23:29 25:11, 25 26:31]], [[Rom.1.32|Rom.1:32]]; absol., [[Rev.16.6|Rev.16:6]] (MM, _VGT_, see word).†
(AS)
